                                "sense_id": "5f4f9a2b-7aab-3788-b92b-c60a8f608f38",
                                "text": "As I have already indicated, however, there is reason to think that at least some of the principles that Kant takes to be synthetic a priori are instead unobviously analytic, and so I shall assume that if Kant shows that a principle associated with one of his categories is unobviously analytic, that too shows that the category is objectively valid."
